	"description" : "Old Japanese woodblock print that's quietly come alive\n\n[h2]Settings[/h2]\n[list]\n[*][b]Background[/b]: the colour around the print.\n[*][b]Speed[/b]: how fast everything moves (0 = still).\n[*][b]Wind[/b]: how much the pines and plants sway (0 = still).\n[*][b]Water[/b]: the lake, the boat and its sail (0 = still).\n[*][b]Sky[/b]: how much the sky drifts (0 = still).\n[*][b]Wildlife[/b]: the crane, dragonfly and fish (0 = none, 75 and up = two cranes).\n[*][b]Render scale[/b]: lower it to save GPU on 4K screens or older cards.\n[/list]\nBrightness, contrast and colour are in Wallpaper Engine's own colour options. The frame rate follows its FPS setting.\n\n[h2]Video[/h2]\nhttps://youtu.be/M3nPVh6UuDc",
